    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0565" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.4016/507: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-24T18:00:00-04:00">September 24, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Department informed by Dr. Stephen Wise<anchor n="53" xml:id="d429-f1"/> that
                    during past 4 days physical violence unrestrained by adequate police measures
                    has been directed against Jews and Jewish business in Warsaw.</p>
                <p>For assistance in reply to Dr. Wise Department requests immediate brief
                    telegraphic report on situation.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d429-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d429-f1" n="53" xml:id="d429-f1-content">
                <p>By telegram of September 23, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d429-f2" n="54" xml:id="d429-f2-content">
                <p>A reply, not printed, was sent to Dr. Wise on October 1, following receipt of
                    telegram No. 114, September 25, from the Ambassador, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
